{"date":"2026-11-22","caps":[[0.05,"Arnie Jordan here, coming to you from row three at Jordan Arena, with the Rinkside Report."],[4.93,"Sunday, November twenty-second. My nephew delivered the whiteboard."],[8.57,"It came with one marker, with about forty minutes of ink, for three games of hockey."],[13.13,"You see where this is going. And yes, that's something on my lip. We'll get to it."],[18.21,"The early game, the RegattaSport Nordiques at the J.E. Culp Habs. Brian Culp opened it."],[23.07,"A Culp scoring for the Culp Habs."],[24.95,"Then Moorzey tied it, Lawrence scored, and Lawrence scored again, with Commish helping on all three."],[30.53,"Commish, three assists in the first and not a point after. Punched out at intermission."],[35.39,"KP got one back, and Pulo made it four to two."],[38.63,"Moorzey made it five to two in the second. I drew a little trophy on the whiteboard. Big mistake. Dixon scored."],[44.62,"JMAC came out for Trigg, and Cooke scored all by himself."],[47.73,"Then the Nordiques got caught with too many men, Moorzey sat for it, and Clark scored on the power play, from Greg Penney and Cooke."],[54.84,"Five all. Moorzey, five points on the night, and one power play for the other team."],[59.99,"In the third, Langlois put the Nordiques back up."],[62.71,"Then Lawrence and Brian Culp went off for roughing at the exact same second, and while they sat, Rob DeBolster scored."],[69.19,"Seven to five Nordiques, final. Levar went the distance in the Habs net, and it was a long distance."],[74.7,"Trophy erased. The Nordiques are eight and oh."],[77.89,"Here's a question for the comments under this report on the league website."],[81.82,"Nordiques, was blowing a five to two lead part of the plan?"],[84.92,"Habs, how do you come back from three down and still lose? I read every comment, and I write back."],[90.67,"Game two, the Timbit Senators at The Keg Canucks. Obie opened it, and Pundy tied it."],[95.34,"Then the penalty box got busy: Rids, Snihur, McMillan and Schmidt, all in two minutes."],[100.13,"Then I knocked my coffee onto the whiteboard and wiped out the first period. Didn't matter. It was one all."],[106.69,"Halfway through the second, both teams changed goalies at the exact same second. Buynink out, Shannon in."],[112.14,"Rennie out, The Plug in. I'm calling it the goalie square dance. Swing your partner, out you go."],[117.74,"Obie put the Senators ahead, then went off for roughing."],[120.75,"Rids went off for hooking again, and Tweedy scored on the power play. Two all."],[124.91,"Rids, two hooks, one goal against. You're fishing in the wrong pond."],[128.55,"Adam Short scored, and Goodie made it four to two."],[131.24,"Then Tourcotte went off for hooking, and Davies scored short-handed anyway. Down a man, the Senators score."],[136.94,"Four to three Canucks, final, two wins in a row!"],[139.53,"Obie, two goals, an assist and a roughing call, and still nothing to show for it."],[144.46,"The late game, Dawson's Oilers at the ColdBreak Leafs."],[147.47,"Parsons opened it, and Pierce scored with nine seconds left in the first. Two nothing Leafs."],[152.55,"I wrote LEAFS LEAD in big letters. You'd think I'd learn."],[156.35,"In the second, NoPants got one back."],[158.34,"Then Steele went off for slashing, and the Oilers scored twice on the power play, forty-one seconds apart."],[164.11,"Craigy, then McPherson. Steele, you set up the first goal of the game and then two more for the other team."],[169.94,"Three to two Oilers."],[171.7,"Then the square dance again!"],[173.37,"Raimondo out, Dawson in, Mallet out, Rosie in, and NoPants off for slashing, all on the same second."],[179.17,"McPherson scored late in the period, four to two, and my marker started squeaking."],[184.59,"In the third, Steele went off again, roughing, with Derrick DeBolster."],[188.38,"Six minutes for Steele, tied with Rids for the most in the building. Then McPherson scored."],[193.3,"Then McPherson scored again, fifty seconds later."],[195.97,"Pierce got one back with fifty-nine seconds left, and it ended six to three."],[200.09,"Pierce, nine seconds left, fifty-nine seconds left. Somebody tell him there's a middle part."],[205.69,"McPherson, four goals again. Last week, four and a loss. This week, four and the boat stayed up."],[210.93,"Craigy was on five of the six Oiler goals. Craigy, I've seen fellas pass less at a potluck."],[215.9,"And the marker died. The last three goals went on a napkin."],[219.77,"Now, about the lip. Yes, that's a moustache."],[222.16,"I grew it for Movember, to raise a little awareness and a few dollars for men's health, and my nephew says it looks like a caterpillar that gave up halfway across."],[230.86,"Here's the serious part, fellas."],[232.61,"Men die on average about four and a half years earlier than women, largely for reasons that could have been prevented, and about one in eight men will be diagnosed with prostate cancer in his lifetime."],[243.34,"So book that check-up you keep putting off, and check in on the fella beside you on the bench."],[248.38,"If you want to chip in, the link is in the comments under this report on the league website."],[253.97,"The big board, eight games in."],[255.73,"McPherson leads the scoring with twenty-four points, Moorzey is right behind him with twenty-three, and KP and Pierce are tied for third with twenty."],[264.28,"In net, Dawson is on top at three twenty-four, Trigg is second at three thirty, and JMAC is third at three seventy-six."],[271.11,"In the standings, the Nordiques are eight and oh, sixteen points, still perfect."],[275.72,"The Oilers have eleven, the Habs and Leafs have seven, the Senators six, and the Canucks four."],[281.13,"Look out, everybody. Well. Look a little bit out."],[284.59,"One more for the comments."],[286.09,"Who gets the hot dog of the week: McPherson for scoring four, or Craigy for setting up four?"],[291.24,"Make your case under this report on the league website. I read every one, and I write back."],[296.96,"So that's your week. Twenty-eight goals, two square dances, and one dead marker."],[301.35,"My nephew says next week, a laptop. I don't trust anything I can't spill coffee on."],[305.9,"If I got your name wrong, or gave your goal to the fella beside you, take it up with the refs, the timekeeper, and how fast you guys skate out there."],[314.02,"This has been Arnie Jordan with the Rinkside Report."]],"pages":[["ROW 3 - 11/22","whiteboard: YES","markers: 1","ink: 40 min??","lip: no comment"],["NORDS 4 HABS 2","Commish: 3 A","then punched out"],["NORDS 5 HABS 2","trophy drawn :)","!Moorzey: too many","HABS 5 NORDS 5"],["NORDS 7 HABS 5","!Lawrence + Culp","!same second","trophy: erased","NORDS 8-0"],["Q: blew a 5-2 lead?","-> comments!"],["G2: Sens @ Canucks","Sens 1 - Canucks 1","Obie 2G 1A!!","Pundy 1G","!Rids: hooking +1 more"],["GOALIE SQUARE DANCE","Buynink -> Shannon","Rennie -> The Plug","swing yr partner"],["CANUCKS 4 SENS 3","!Rids: 2 hooks","Davies: SH goal","CANUCKS: 2 IN A ROW"],["LEAFS 2 OIL 0","LEAFS LEAD","(I never learn)"],["!Steele - slash","= 2 PP goals agst","OIL 3 LEAFS 2"],["SQUARE DANCE #2","marker squeaking"],["OIL 6 LEAFS 3","McPherson: 4 G","Pierce: 0:09, 0:59","!Steele: 6 min"],["Craigy: 1 G 4 A","marker: DEAD","(napkin)"],["MOVEMBER","the 'stache: yes","book a check-up!","check on yr buddies"],["McPherson 24","Moorzey 23","KP/Pierce 20","Dawson 3.24 GAA","NORDS 8-0 16 pts"],["HOT DOG OF THE WEEK?","McPherson or Craigy","-> comments!"],["28 goals","2 square dances","1 dead marker","nxt wk: laptop??"]],"sleeper":{"team":"TML","seed":5624},"kf":[{"t":18.21,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":1200,"h":0,"a":0,"goal":null,"final":false},{"t":21.25,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":862,"h":1,"a":0,"goal":"CULP","final":false},{"t":25.23,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":688,"h":1,"a":1,"goal":"MOORZEY","final":false},{"t":26.17,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":642,"h":1,"a":2,"goal":"LAWRENCE","final":false},{"t":27.33,"g":0,"per":"1","clk":323,"h":1,"a":3,"goal":"LAWRENCE","f